{
  "description": "#5667 — the three MCP agent commands: `create_mcp_agent` and `revoke_mcp_agent` through the command leg, `list_mcp_agents` as the read that observes them. `mcp_agents` is device-local and outside the snapshot, and each stack mints a created agent's id, token and `created_at_ms`, so the list is keyed by name (unique in any letter case) and the create's return names only what the caller chose. `seed.mcp_agents` exists for the one thing a created agent cannot give both stacks: an id `revoke_mcp_agent` can name. `create_space` makes `C1` so a create can grant a LIVE space: only that op moves the snapshot. Each granted space is its own `space_ids` segment, so `C1` relabels like any id-valued attribute; `GONE` is a seeded grant whose space no longer exists, which grants nothing and lists as stored. The refusals run in the backend's order: the name, then the space list, then the name clash its `ON CONFLICT(name)` finds.",
